\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces All four submitted configurations on the PlantCLEF 2026 hidden test set (public Macro F1). The cRT pivot is strongly negative; the genus rerank and the phenology prior move the anchor by $-0.006$ and $-0.005$ respectively, magnitudes small (about two to three times the run-to-run leaderboard noise floor we characterise at ${\sim }0.002$) but consistent in sign. We read this as the BioCLIP 2.5 posterior implicitly absorbing both signals through training-distribution co-occurrence; the orthogonality argument is developed in \S  \ref {sec:orthogonality}.}}{13}{table.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:summary}{{6}{13}{All four submitted configurations on the PlantCLEF 2026 hidden test set (public Macro F1). The cRT pivot is strongly negative; the genus rerank and the phenology prior move the anchor by $-0.006$ and $-0.005$ respectively, magnitudes small (about two to three times the run-to-run leaderboard noise floor we characterise at ${\sim }0.002$) but consistent in sign. We read this as the BioCLIP 2.5 posterior implicitly absorbing both signals through training-distribution co-occurrence; the orthogonality argument is developed in \S \ref {sec:orthogonality}}{table.6}{}}
